"""Application questions independent of the ten lesson checks."""
Q=[
('A team signs DQ after reviewing drawings. Which statement can its conclusion support?',['Installed performance was demonstrated under production conditions','Proposed design suitability was evaluated within the stated scope','Routine production is authorized for every planned product'],1,'Limit the conclusion to the evidence and scope of the design review.'),
('The URS has revision 3 but the DQ matrix cites revision 2. What is needed?',['Assess changed requirements and reconcile the review baseline','Keep revision 2 because the matrix was already formatted','Replace the revision label without checking affected conclusions'],0,'A revision change can alter the design-review basis.'),
('A vendor guarantees a catalogue maximum volume; the process minimum is undefined. What remains unresolved?',['Only the purchase order approval date','Only the number of instruments on the drawing','Suitability across the intended operating volume range'],2,'Supplier capability cannot define the missing process need.'),
('A fictional indication requirement is ±0.5 °C. Three applicable component bounds are ±0.2 °C each. Which conservative total applies?',['±0.2 °C','±0.6 °C','±0.4 °C'],1,'The aligned worst-case sum is 0.2 + 0.2 + 0.2 = 0.6 °C, not a full uncertainty budget.'),
('The vendor proposes ±0.1, ±0.1 and ±0.2 °C components. Against the fictional ±0.5 °C limit, what follows?',['The 0.4 °C sum supports further design review, subject to applicability','The 0.4 °C sum proves installed accuracy at all process conditions','The 0.4 °C sum establishes a complete measurement uncertainty budget'],0,'The conservative sum is within the teaching limit, but conditions and later verification remain relevant.'),
('A gasket has a known material name but no product/cleaning compatibility basis. What is justified?',['Close suitability because the material identity is recorded','Close suitability because the vessel body is stainless steel','Request evidence relevant to the intended exposure conditions'],2,'Identity is necessary evidence but does not alone prove suitability.'),
('An outlet drawing is revised to remove a retained pocket. Which closure is strongest?',['Reference the reviewed revision and retain installed/cleaning verification','Mark the issue closed from the supplier email subject line','Delete the original finding because the drawing was replaced'],0,'The closure needs reviewed evidence and must retain future verification obligations.'),
('A control loop and its alarm use a common transmitter. What should the DQ review examine?',['Whether each display has a different instrument label','Whether shared failures undermine the proposed protection','Whether both displays have the same enclosure colour'],1,'Evaluate the failure mechanism rather than counting devices or labels.'),
('A fault response inhibits heating, but restart behaviour is unspecified. What action fits DQ?',['Approve the design because shutdown is the only relevant state','Allow unrestricted restart and investigate after routine operation','Request justified recovery behaviour and link it to verification'],2,'Recovery can affect risk and must be addressed as relevant to intended use.'),
('A password is shown on the control screen. What does it demonstrate by itself?',['A complete compliant audit trail and retention system','Only the presence of an access feature, not adequate system control','Independent authorization for all changes to process settings'],1,'A login feature does not establish full access, record or computerized-system compliance.'),
('A rear instrument cannot be removed after piping is added. Which input was missed?',['Maintenance access in the installed arrangement','The arithmetic average of the supplier error bounds','The number of signed pages in the purchase package'],0,'Review access with the relevant installed configuration and dimensions.'),
('A utility is qualified for its own scope. What else supports a vessel connection?',['A second copy of the utility report with a new cover','A statement that qualified utilities fit every receiving system','A comparison of supply conditions with vessel design needs'],2,'System qualification does not automatically establish interface compatibility.'),
('An action owner is assigned for a protective-control gap. How should evidence status change?',['Move to demonstrated control because someone owns the action','Remain unresolved until suitable evidence is reviewed','Move to routine-use ready if the due date is near'],1,'Ownership and schedule are management information, not evidence of effectiveness.'),
('A low risk total hides a severe effect with uncertain detection. Which response is strongest?',['Examine severity, uncertainty and the basis of the proposed control','Accept the total because multiplication standardizes every risk','Remove the severe effect because its likelihood estimate is low'],0,'A score alone cannot settle an unsupported high-consequence scenario.'),
('The supplier protocol omits an identified sensor-failure challenge. Which action is appropriate?',['Approve it because supplier protocols take precedence over site procedures','Repeat the normal-operation test instead of addressing the failure','Arrange site suitability review and a justified verification supplement'],2,'The site must assess protocol suitability and coverage of relevant verification needs.'),
('A FAT result is proposed for reuse after a design change. Which question matters most?',['Is its configuration/function still applicable after the change?','Was the report produced before the invoice was approved?','Does the supplier use the same document template at every site?'],0,'Evidence reuse depends on applicable configuration, conditions and impacts, not presentation.'),
('A required gasket specification is changed during DQ. What preserves traceability?',['Update only the vendor contact list and delivery date','Retain the prior baseline and assess affected conclusions','Remove earlier records to avoid conflicting design versions'],1,'Controlled history and impact review allow the decision to be reconstructed.'),
('A proposed next activity is unrelated to an open design gap. What supports progression?',['An overall project completion percentage above 80%','An informal supplier promise to fix the gap after use','A documented impact assessment and authorized stage decision'],2,'Progression is specific to the proposed activity and does not close the design finding.'),
('Eight design rows are supported and two remain open. What is the numerical coverage?',['20%','80%','100%'],1,'8/10 × 100 = 80%; this does not establish suitability or a release threshold.'),
('What should accompany a DQ package handed to the IQ team?',['Only the final signature page and purchase order','Only the latest vendor brochure and delivery checklist','Controlled design baseline, findings and verification dependencies'],2,'IQ needs the accepted design basis and visibility of unresolved dependencies.')]
QUESTIONS=[dict(question=q,options=o,answer=a,feedback=f) for q,o,a,f in Q]
